{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>For YHWH will judge His people.</b> He will take the case of His people from them, like שפטני אלהים (Elohim has judged me) and ריבה ריבי (plead my cause)." "<b>Yitnaḥem.</b> I have explained it." "<b>Azat yad.</b> The azat yad of Israel, and the meaning is strength, and the tav stands in place of the heh, for both are feminine markers. So too ושבת לנשיא (she shall return to her husband)." "<b>And none shut up or left.</b> When the captives are many, some are taken from them and some left behind. And now, nearly all is lost."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:26:11.710649955Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}